#. from gnome:reviewed/gnumeric/master/help
#: C/gnumeric.xml:24
msgid ""
"A text element can contain a series of letters, numbers or other contents. "
"For example, the first cell in a worksheet might contain the characters "
"—This worksheet describes the company's income — which "
"<application>Gnumeric</application> would interpret to be text. In order to "
"distinguish text elements from number or formula elements, the text element "
"may start with a single quote. For instance, if a cell contained only the "
"three digits 345, <application>Gnumeric</application> would consider that to"
" be the number three hundred and forty five. If this cell is intended to be "
"a string, <application>Gnumeric</application> will store the cell as '345. "
"The newline character cannot be entered directly but must be entered as "
"<keycombo> <keycap>Alt</keycap> <keycap>Enter</keycap></keycombo>. For more "
"information on entering and formatting text elements, see <xref "
"linkend=\"sect-data-text\"/>."
msgstr ""
"Ett textelement kan bestå av bokstäver, siffror eller annat innehåll. Den "
"första cellen i ett kalkylblad kan till exempel innehålla texten ”Det här "
"kalkylbladet beskriver företagets intäkter”, som "
"<application>Gnumeric</application> tolkar som text. För att skilja "
"textelement från tal och formler kan texten inledas med en apostrof. Om en "
"cell till exempel bara innehåller siffrorna 345 tolkar "
"<application>Gnumeric</application> dem som talet trehundrafyrtiofem. Om "
"cellen i stället ska innehålla text lagrar "
"<application>Gnumeric</application> den som '345. Radbrytningar kan inte "
"matas in direkt, utan infogas med tangentkombinationen <keycombo> "
"<keycap>Alt</keycap> <keycap>Enter</keycap></keycombo>. Mer information om "
"hur du matar in och formaterar text finns i <xref linkend=\"sect-data-"
"text\"/>."

#. from gnome:reviewed/gnumeric/master/help
#: C/gnumeric.xml:51
msgid ""
"A number element can contain a series of digits (425) but may include "
"specific text and formatting characters to indicate negative numbers (-345),"
" decimal separator (34.0567), thousand separators (12,342), currency ($23), "
"dates (21-10-1998), times (10:23) or scientific notation (2.3e12). Dates may"
" include the names of months or their abbreviation. The currency, decimal "
"separator and thousands separator symbols vary depending on the locale (the "
"language and other location specific behaviour) to which "
"<application>Gnumeric</application> has been set. See <xref linkend=\"sect-"
"configuration-localization\"/> to understand how to change the locale. If "
"you want a number to be displayed as a plain string without any number "
"formatting, you can put a single quote (') before it. For more information "
"on entering and formatting, numeric elements see <xref linkend=\"sect-data-"
"numbers\"/>."
msgstr ""
"Ett talelement kan bestå av siffror, som 425, och särskilda tecken för att "
"visa exempelvis negativa tal (-345), decimalavgränsare (34.0567), "
"tusentalsavgränsare (12,342), valuta ($23), datum (1998-10-21), klockslag "
"(10:23) eller vetenskaplig notation (2.3e12). Datum kan innehålla månadsnamn"
" eller förkortningar. Valuta-, decimal- och tusentalsavgränsare varierar "
"beroende på lokalen (språk och andra platsinställningar) som används i "
"<application>Gnumeric</application>. Se <xref linkend=\"sect-configuration-"
"localization\"/> om hur du ändrar lokalen. Om ett tal ska visas som vanlig "
"text utan talformatering kan du inleda det med en apostrof ('). Mer "
"information om hur du matar in och formaterar tal finns i <xref "
"linkend=\"sect-data-numbers\"/>."

#. from gnome:reviewed/gnumeric/master/help
#: C/gnumeric.xml:77
msgid ""
"A boolean element can contain one of two values: TRUE and FALSE. These are "
"useful as inputs or outputs from formulas and for boolean algebra. More "
"information on boolean data elements is presented in <xref linkend=\"sect-"
"data-boolean\"/>."
msgstr ""
"Ett booleskt element kan ha ett av två värden: TRUE eller FALSE. Dessa "
"värden används som indata eller resultat i formler och inom boolesk algebra."
" Mer information om booleska dataelement finns i <xref linkend=\"sect-data-"
"boolean\"/>."

#. from gnome:reviewed/gnumeric/master/help
#: C/gnumeric.xml:91
msgid ""
"A formula is an instruction to <application>Gnumeric</application> which "
"describes a calculation which should be performed automatically. These "
"formulas can contain standard arithmetic elements but can also contain "
"references to other cells. Calculations which depend on other cells are "
"usually recalculated when the values of another cell changes. Formulas "
"always begin with a special character — the equals sign (=). The commercial "
"at symbol (@) can be used instead of the equals sign during data entry but "
"<application>Gnumeric</application> will convert this to an equals sign. "
"Alternatively, an entry which describes a calculation and which starts with "
"either the plus (+) or minus symbol (-) will be converted to a formula "
"starting with an equals sign. For a more complete explanation of formulas, "
"see <xref linkend=\"sect-data-formulas\"/>."
msgstr ""
"En formel är en instruktion som anger vilken beräkning "
"<application>Gnumeric</application> ska utföra automatiskt. Formler kan "
"innehålla vanliga räkneoperationer och referenser till andra celler. "
"Beräkningar som beror på andra celler räknas vanligen om när värdet i någon "
"av dessa celler ändras. Formler börjar alltid med likhetstecknet (=). Under "
"inmatning kan tecknet @ användas i stället, men "
"<application>Gnumeric</application> omvandlar det till ett likhetstecken. "
"Även en inmatning som börjar med plus (+) eller minus (-) omvandlas till en "
"formel som börjar med likhetstecken. En utförligare förklaring av formler "
"finns i <xref linkend=\"sect-data-formulas\"/>."

#. from gnome:reviewed/gnumeric/master/help
#: C/gnumeric.xml:111
msgid ""
"A cell reference is the part of a formula which refers to another cell. For "
"example, in the formula to add two cells =(A4+A1), both A4 and A1 are cell "
"references. These references can be quite complex referring to cells in "
"different worksheets or even in different files. See <xref linkend=\"sect-"
"data-formulas-references\"/> for a complete explanation of references."
msgstr ""
"En cellreferens är den del av en formel som hänvisar till en annan cell. I "
"formeln =(A4+A1), som summerar två celler, är både A4 och A1 cellreferenser."
" Referenser kan vara mer komplicerade och peka på celler i andra kalkylblad "
"eller till och med i andra filer. En fullständig förklaring finns i <xref "
"linkend=\"sect-data-formulas-references\"/>."

#. from gnome:reviewed/gnumeric/master/help
#: C/gnumeric.xml:128
msgid ""
"An error element describes the failure to calculate the result of a formula."
" These values are rarely entered directly by a user but usually are the "
"display given when a formula cannot be correctly calculated. See <xref "
"linkend=\"sect-data-errors\"/> for a complete list of error values and their"
" explanation."
msgstr ""
"Ett felvärde anger att resultatet av en formel inte kunde beräknas. "
"Användaren skriver sällan in sådana värden direkt; de visas vanligen när en "
"formel inte kan beräknas korrekt. En fullständig lista över felvärden och "
"deras betydelse finns i <xref linkend=\"sect-data-errors\"/>."

#. from gnome:reviewed/gnumeric/master/help
#: C/gnumeric.xml:16
msgid ""
"The five basic types of data which can be stored in a spreadsheet cell are: "
"<_:variablelist-1/>"
msgstr ""
"De fem grundläggande datatyper som kan lagras i en kalkylbladscell är: "
"<_:variablelist-1/>"

#. from gnome:reviewed/gnumeric/master/help
#: C/gnumeric.xml:143
msgid ""
"A cell may display a series of hash marks (######). This indicates that the "
"result is too wide to display in the cell given the current font setting and"
" the current column width. When this occurs, the value in the cell can be "
"seen in two ways. If the cell is selected, the value will appear in the data"
" entry area (to the right of the equals button directly above the cell "
"grid). Alternatively, the column containing the cell can be widened until "
"the data contents become visible: select the whole column (by clicking on "
"the column header) and choose <menuchoice> <guimenu>Format</guimenu> "
"<guisubmenu>Column</guisubmenu> <guimenuitem>Auto fit "
"selection</guimenuitem> </menuchoice>."
msgstr ""
"En cell kan visa flera nummertecken (######). Det betyder att resultatet är "
"för brett för att visas med den aktuella teckenstorleken och kolumnbredden. "
"Du kan se cellens värde på två sätt. Markera cellen så visas värdet i "
"inmatningsfältet, till höger om likhetsteckenknappen ovanför cellrutnätet. "
"Du kan också bredda kolumnen tills innehållet syns: markera hela kolumnen "
"genom att klicka på kolumnrubriken och välj <menuchoice> "
"<guimenu>Format</guimenu> <guisubmenu>Kolumn</guisubmenu> "
"<guimenuitem>Autopassa markering</guimenuitem> </menuchoice>."

#. from gnome:reviewed/gnumeric/master/help
#: C/gnumeric.xml:166
msgid ""
"Text elements consist of an arbitrary sequence of characters or numbers "
"entered into a cell. Because <application>Gnumeric</application> "
"automatically recognizes certain sequences as numbers or formulas, certain "
"sequences of characters (such as sequences containing only digits or a text "
"element which starts with an equals sign) must be treated specially to have "
"them considered text. In order to force any sequence to be considered text, "
"the sequence can be started with an apostrophe symbol (<keysym>'</keysym>). "
"Alternatively, the 'number' format of the cell can be specified to be 'text'"
" before entering the characters, as explained in <xref linkend=\"number-"
"formatting-overview\"/>. Text elements are the simplest elements to enter "
"into spreadsheet cells."
msgstr ""
"Textelement består av en valfri följd tecken eller siffror som matas in i en"
" cell. Eftersom <application>Gnumeric</application> automatiskt känner igen "
"vissa följder som tal eller formler måste vissa inmatningar behandlas "
"särskilt för att tolkas som text, till exempel en följd som bara innehåller "
"siffror eller börjar med ett likhetstecken. Inled inmatningen med en "
"apostrof (<keysym>'</keysym>) för att tvinga den att tolkas som text. Du kan"
" också ändra cellens talformat till ”text” innan du skriver in tecknen, "
"enligt beskrivningen i <xref linkend=\"number-formatting-overview\"/>. "
"Textelement är det enklaste att mata in i kalkylbladsceller."

#. from gnome:reviewed/gnumeric/master/help
#: C/gnumeric.xml:182
msgid ""
"An example of a spreadsheet cell grid with cells containing text is given in"
" <xref linkend=\"fig-cell-with-text\"/>. <_:figure-1/>"
msgstr ""
"<xref linkend=\"fig-cell-with-text\"/> visar ett exempel på ett cellrutnät "
"med text i cellerna. <_:figure-1/>"

#. from gnome:reviewed/gnumeric/master/help
#: C/gnumeric.xml:196
msgid ""
"Valid text entries include simple words, whole sentences and even "
"paragraphs."
msgstr ""
"Text kan bestå av enstaka ord, hela meningar eller till och med stycken."

#. from gnome:reviewed/gnumeric/master/help
#: C/gnumeric.xml:202
msgid ""
"To include a newline in a cell, a special key combination is required. A "
"newline symbol can be inserted with the key combination of "
"<keycombo><keysym>Alt</keysym><keysym>Enter</keysym></keycombo>."
msgstr ""
"Du behöver en särskild tangentkombination för att infoga en radbrytning i en"
" cell. Använd "
"<keycombo><keysym>Alt</keysym><keysym>Enter</keysym></keycombo>."

#. from gnome:reviewed/gnumeric/master/help
#: C/gnumeric.xml:218
msgid ""
"Number data elements include a variety of data all of which are stored and "
"manipulated by <application>Gnumeric</application> as numbers. This includes"
" integers, decimal fractions, general fractions, numbers in scientific "
"notation, dates, times, and currency values."
msgstr ""
"Talelement omfattar flera slags värden som "
"<application>Gnumeric</application> lagrar och bearbetar som tal: heltal, "
"decimaltal, vanliga bråk, tal i vetenskaplig notation, datum, klockslag och "
"valutavärden."

#. from gnome:reviewed/gnumeric/master/help
#: C/gnumeric.xml:226
msgid ""
"Data are recognized as numbers when they are entered, dependent on the "
"format of the sequence of characters entered. "
"<application>Gnumeric</application> attempts to intelligently guess the "
"subtype of the data and match the data to an existing format for numbered "
"data. If it matches a data format, <application>Gnumeric</application> will "
"automatically assign the datum to a data type and associate an appropriate "
"display format with the cell. The format recognition of "
"<application>Gnumeric</application> includes a wide variety of data formats "
"which are discussed in detail in <xref linkend=\"number-formatting-"
"overview\"/>."
msgstr ""
"Inmatade data tolkas som tal beroende på hur tecknen är formaterade. "
"<application>Gnumeric</application> försöker avgöra vilken undertyp data har"
" och matcha dem mot ett befintligt talformat. Om ett format känns igen "
"tilldelar <application>Gnumeric</application> automatiskt data en datatyp "
"och kopplar ett lämpligt visningsformat till cellen. "
"<application>Gnumeric</application> känner igen många olika format, som "
"beskrivs närmare i <xref linkend=\"number-formatting-overview\"/>."
